    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0674" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/663: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gwynn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-22T14:00:00+02:00">October 22, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—12:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>406. With reference to my telegram 307 of August 25, noon and despatch No. 457 of
                    same date,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d778-f1"/> I have received a note from the
                    Lebanese Minister for Foreign Affairs stating that the Council of Ministers at
                    its meeting of October 7, 1942 decided to exonerate the American philanthropic,
                    educational and religious institutions from all municipal and customs taxes in
                    conformity with the treaties and conventions in force.</p>
                <p>The tenor of this note is very similar to that of the Syrian decree reported in
                    my 340, September 12, 9 a.m. and would appear scarcely to satisfy the request
                    contained in the informal <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> I left with
                    the Lebanese Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gwynn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d778-f1" n="31" xml:id="d778-f1-content">
